Let $X$ be a smooth geometrically integral variety over $K$. A \textbf{positive linear torsor presentation} of $X$ consisists of datum $(G,V,Y,q,\lambda)$, where

1. $G$ denotes a connected linear algebraic group or a group of multiplicative type;

2. $V$ is an affine space equipped with a linear $G$-action $\rho:G\to \mathrm{GL}(V)$; 

3. $Y\subset V$ a $G$-invariant open subscheme with $\mathrm{codim}_{V}(V-Y)\geq 2$; 

4. $q:Y\to X$ a $G$-torsor;

5. $\lambda:\mathbb{G}_{m}\to Z(G)$ a central cocharacter such that all weights of $\lambda$ on $V$ are positive.

\label{P^1-connected}
Let $X/K$ be a smooth geometrically integral variety over a field of characteristic 0. Assume that $X$ admits a positive linear torsor presentation $(G,V,Y,q,\lambda)$. For $x_,y\in X(K)$, the following are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
\renewcommand{(\roman{enumi})}{(\roman{enumi})}
\item $\delta_q(x)=\delta_q(y)$ in $H^1(K,G)$;
\item both $x$ and $y$ have lifts in $Y^\xi(K)$ for one twist $q^{\xi}:Y^{\xi}\to X$;
\item $x\sim_{\mathbb{P}^1} y$;
\item $x\sim_{\mathbb{P}^1,\mathrm{ch}} y$.
\end{enumerate}

Moreover, $\delta_{q}$ is surjective and induces a bijection of sets:
\[
X(K)/\sim_{\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathrm{ch}}\cong H^1(K,G).
\]
